{"title":"2024 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 11","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_11\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 11</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_11\">Problem 11</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 11\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>How many ordered pairs of integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/b/98b7e4c455672c30d743cce7506408a40cb68129.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(m, n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"18\" /> satisfy <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/9/709d4b3e60a425cc1d9afea9abea4cd9dac73495.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{n^2-49}=m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"116\" height=\"21\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/8/2d81f6fd51d2b77fa449c25b21f09c8883850bea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }1 \\qquad\\textbf{(B) }2 \\qquad\\textbf{(C) }3 \\qquad\\textbf{(D) }4 \\qquad\\textbf{(E) }\\text{infinitely many}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"455\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Square and rearrange to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/a/46a52135dff6f461d4e6972de3258a661885f18e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[49 = n^2-m^2 = (n-m)(n+m)\\]\" width=\"255\" height=\"20\" /> Remembering the negatives, we can choose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/c/34c8e6bf4d57cd6f2bb0d7d43e00f0f442f53b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$49$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" />, for solutions \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/d/84de65ed469aeb0042accda72e2fbb412298da2a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(n, m) = (25, 24), (7, 0), (25, -24), (-25, 24), (-7, 0), (-25, -24)\\]\" width=\"496\" height=\"18\" /> But <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> must be nonnegative, so we can discard two of the solutions for the answer of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/0/e40af792bb8c6fd11211a2eee10e525fc7841b4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"56\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are 4 ordered pairs of integers \\((m, n)\\) that satisfy the equation, which corresponds to option (D).\nStep-by-Step Solution\n1. Understand the Constraints\nGiven the equation:\n\\(\\sqrt{n^{2}-49}=m\\)\nSince \\(m\\) is equal to a principal (positive) square root, \\(m\\) must be a non-negative integer (\\(m \\ge 0\\)).\n2. Algebraic Rearrangement\nSquare both sides to eliminate the radical:\n\\(n^{2}-49=m^{2}\\)Move \\(m^{2}\\) to the left side:\n\\(n^{2}-m^{2}=49\\)\n3. Factor using Difference of Squares\n\\((n-m)(n+m)=49\\)\n4. Find Factor Pairs of 49\nSince \\(m\\) and \\(n\\) are integers, \\((n - m)\\) and \\((n + m)\\) must be integer factors of \\(49\\). The pairs of factors that multiply to \\(49\\) are:\n\t• \\((1, 49)\\) and \\((49, 1)\\)\n\t• \\((-1, -49)\\) and \\((-49, -1)\\)\n\t• \\((7, 7)\\) and \\((-7, -7)\\)\n5. Solve for \\(m\\) and \\(n\\)\nWe can find \\(m\\) by subtracting the first factor from the second:\n\\((n+m)-(n-m)=2m\\)Let's check each pair of factors to find solutions where \\(m \\ge 0\\):\n\t• Case 1: \\(n - m = 1\\) and \\(n + m = 49\\)\n\\(2m=49-1=48\\implies m=24\\)\n\\(n=25\\)\n👉 Valid Pair: \\((24, 25)\\)\n\t• Case 2: \\(n - m = -49\\) and \\(n + m = -1\\)\n\\(2m=-1-(-49)=48\\implies m=24\\)\n\\(n=-25\\)\n👉 Valid Pair: \\((24, -25)\\)\n\t• Case 3: \\(n - m = 7\\) and \\(n + m = 7\\)\n\\(2m=7-7=0\\implies m=0\\)\n\\(n=7\\)\n👉 Valid Pair: \\((0, 7)\\)\n\t• Case 4: \\(n - m = -7\\) and \\(n + m = -7\\)\n\\(2m=-7-(-7)=0\\implies m=0\\)\n\\(n=-7\\)\n👉 Valid Pair: \\((0, -7)\\)\n(Note: The other combinations yield negative values for \\(m\\), which violates \\(m \\ge 0\\).)\nConclusion\nThe complete set of integer solutions is \\(\\{(24, 25), (24, -25), (0, 7), (0, -7)\\}\\), making a total of 4 pairs.\n</p><p>Taarun Dinesh kumar\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A\" title=\"2024 AMC 10A\">2024 AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2024 AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2024 AMC 10A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2023 AMC 10B Problems\">2023 AMC 10B Problems</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2024 AMC 10B Problems\">2024 AMC 10B Problems</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2024 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2024 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2024 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems